Package: wlboard
Version: 0.1.0-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Aleksander Kutycki <74899889+olekkut@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/olekkut/wlboard
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.35)
Recommends: fonts-dejavu-core | fonts-noto-core
Description: Lightweight, customizable native Wayland floating virtual keyboard
 wlboard is a native Wayland floating on-screen virtual keyboard written in
 Rust. It uses zwlr_layer_shell_v1 so it floats on top without stealing focus
 on KDE Plasma, Hyprland, and Sway, supports automatic zwp_virtual_keyboard_v1
 and pure-Rust uinput key injection with a 250 ms stuck-key watchdog, multi-touch
 chording, EN/PL/UA/RU/AR layouts, Standard and Compact for TV modes, KDE Plasma
 D-Bus two-way layout sync, StatusNotifierItem tray, and a built-in Settings and
 User Presets editor.
